<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article (Maybe a tale too? *More in <em>Additional Notes</em>)</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Action, Thriller</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Standard SCP layout with quite some addendums (incident report + psychological report + phone call + several Interviews + operational execution Protocol + some more)</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> My article will tell a story about the SCP Foundation and an SCP struggling to find common ground. SCP-XXXX wants to die, but cant. The Foundation wants to contain it, but is not able to do so. A researcher wants to mediate between these two parties, and pays dearly for the attempt. And with the conflict ongoing, more and more people are being drawn into it.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> SCP-XXXX, one protagonist in the story, has an seemingly simple ability. When dead, its consciousness is transferred in to another body. By that method it is profiting from the knowledge and life experience of every man it has ever bin. Yet it wants to die one last time, tired of the endless life it was gifted, and realises that despite being nearly omniscient, the SCP cant figure out how. In despair it turns to the SCP Foundation that made the fatal error to underrate the SCPs power.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Straightaway it is clear, the SCP Foundation fears SCP-XXXX. But the SCP seems to be completely harmless at its first appearances in the documents. A closer look however reveals, that not its ability is hazardous, but the sheer amount of knowledge it owns about not only science, psychology or self defence, but about the SCP Foundation. Threatened, the Foundation by reflex draws its sword, forgetting that what they attempt to fight is immortal.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> *I, unwisely, already have started a draft without waiting for an reply by qualified reviewers. But when I paused tipping, I noticed that the word counter was already indicating 3000 words (I am not even finished jet), of which only 600 are taken up by the actual SCP document. So I am not only looking for an GREENLIGHT here, but also seek for an experts opinion. Is it just a very long SCP, or would it be better to make it a SCP with an associated Tale. Feel free to ask me for the draft if needed. I do even recommend it for reading, if you need to get a clearer picture of what I tried to sum up in 399 words here.</p>

